 {
  "id": "L23/p1",
  "lesson": "L23",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>What does the 1.5-point gap show?</p>",
  "answer": "b",
  "answerKind": "choice",
  "tol": 0,
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "a",
    "html": "<p>That the new model is better: 1.5 points on 500 items is 7 more correct answers.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "b",
    "html": "<p>Little by itself: each score has a standard error of about 2 points, so the gap is within noise unless a paired, item-by-item comparison shows the models rarely disagree.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "c",
    "html": "<p>That the old model is better, since benchmark gains usually come from contamination.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "d",
    "html": "<p>Nothing at all: accuracy cannot be compared across models.</p>"
   }
  ],
  "explain": "<p>Each accuracy has standard error <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>500</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0205</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{0.7 \\cdot 0.3 / 500} \\approx 0.0205</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.24em;vertical-align:-0.305em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.935em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3.2em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.3/500</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.895em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:1.02em;height:1.28em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.28em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1296\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M263,681c0.7,0,18,39.7,52,119\nc34,79.3,68.167,158.7,102.5,238c34.3,79.3,51.8,119.3,52.5,120\nc340,-704.7,510.7,-1060.3,512,-1067\nl0 -0\nc4.7,-7.3,11,-11,19,-11\nH40000v40H1012.3\ns-271.3,567,-271.3,567c-38.7,80.7,-84,175,-136,283c-52,108,-89.167,185.3,-111.5,232\nc-22.3,46.7,-33.8,70.3,-34.5,71c-4.7,4.7,-12.3,7,-23,7s-12,-1,-12,-1\ns-109,-253,-109,-253c-72.7,-168,-109.3,-252,-110,-252c-10.7,8,-22,16.7,-34,26\nc-22,17.3,-33.3,26,-34,26s-26,-26,-26,-26s76,-59,76,-59s76,-60,76,-60z\nM1001 80h400000v40h-400000z\"></path></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.305em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.0205</span></span></span></span>; for two independent scores the difference has standard error about 0.029, so 1.5 points is half a standard error. Because both models face the same items, a paired comparison removes the variation they share and can be much sharper (exercise 2); the same item-level data also exposes contamination, if the new model does suspiciously well on items found on the web (L16). Without that analysis, the claim is not supported.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "L23/p2",
  "lesson": "L23",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>Two random directions in 100 dimensions have a squared cosine of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/100</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/100</span></span></span></span> on average. What is the typical size of their cosine (the root mean square)?</p>",
  "answer": "0.1",
  "answerKind": "numeric",
  "tol": 0.01,
  "options": [],
  "explain": "<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{1/100} = 0.1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.24em;vertical-align:-0.305em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.935em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3.2em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span class=\"mord\">1/100</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.895em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:1.02em;height:1.28em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.28em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1296\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M263,681c0.7,0,18,39.7,52,119\nc34,79.3,68.167,158.7,102.5,238c34.3,79.3,51.8,119.3,52.5,120\nc340,-704.7,510.7,-1060.3,512,-1067\nl0 -0\nc4.7,-7.3,11,-11,19,-11\nH40000v40H1012.3\ns-271.3,567,-271.3,567c-38.7,80.7,-84,175,-136,283c-52,108,-89.167,185.3,-111.5,232\nc-22.3,46.7,-33.8,70.3,-34.5,71c-4.7,4.7,-12.3,7,-23,7s-12,-1,-12,-1\ns-109,-253,-109,-253c-72.7,-168,-109.3,-252,-110,-252c-10.7,8,-22,16.7,-34,26\nc-22,17.3,-33.3,26,-34,26s-26,-26,-26,-26s76,-59,76,-59s76,-60,76,-60z\nM1001 80h400000v40h-400000z\"></path></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.305em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1</span></span></span></span>: random directions in high dimensions are nearly orthogonal. In a residual stream of a few thousand dimensions the typical overlap is about 0.02, so a model can pack far more directions than dimensions with little interference between features that are rarely active together. This is superposition, and it is why single neurons are often hard to interpret.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "L23/d1/s1",
  "lesson": "L23",
  "kind": "derivation",
  "prompt": "<p class=\"review-context\">The gain from pairing</p><p>Both models score 70%, so each per-item variance is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.7 \\cdot 0.3 = 0.21</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.21</span></span></span></span>. If the correlation between their item scores is 0.6, the paired variance per item is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.42</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.21</mn><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.42 - 2 \\cdot 0.6 \\cdot 0.21 =</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.42</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.21</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <span class=\"blank\" data-blank=\"0\">[ 1 ]</span>.</p>",
